{"title": "Savage Attacker", "pageid": 8373, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Savage_Attacker", "categories": ["Passive features"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote noexcerpt\">Not to be confused with <a href=\"/wiki/Savage_Attacks\" title=\"Savage Attacks\">Savage Attacks</a>        </div>\n\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box bg3wiki-tooltip-gradient-common\">\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Savage_Attacker.webp\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/3/30/Savage_Attacker.webp/300px-Savage_Attacker.webp, /w/images/3/30/Savage_Attacker.webp 1.5x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/30/Savage_Attacker.webp/300px-Savage_Attacker.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/3/30/Savage_Attacker.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>Savage Attacker</b> is a passive feature provided by the <a href=\"/wiki/Feat\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Feat\">feat</a> of the same name. Your attacks become more fierce, and you deal damage at a higher level than usual when dealing melee weapon damage.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\"> Description </span></h2>\n<p>When making melee weapon attacks, you roll your damage dice twice and use the highest result. \n</p>\n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div>\n</div> \n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_learn\"> How to learn </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<p>Granted by the feats:\n<a href=\"/wiki/Savage_Attacker_(Feat)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Savage Attacker (Feat)\">Savage Attacker (Feat)</a>\n</p>\n  <p>Used by creatures:</p><ul style=\"list-style-type: none\"><li>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Bao%27ek%27nuk\" title=\"Bao'ek'nuk\">Bao'ek'nuk</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Bugbear\" title=\"Bugbear\">Bugbear</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Chop\" title=\"Chop\">Chop</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Gilded_Minotaur\" title=\"Gilded Minotaur\">Gilded Minotaur</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Grukkoh\" title=\"Grukkoh\">Grukkoh</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Hairy_Henry\" title=\"Hairy Henry\">Hairy Henry</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Holli_Dylford\" title=\"Holli Dylford\">Holli Dylford</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Lady_Ague\" title=\"Lady Ague\">Lady Ague</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Lady_Flux\" title=\"Lady Flux\">Lady Flux</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Lady_Quinsy\" title=\"Lady Quinsy\">Lady Quinsy</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Minotaur\" title=\"Minotaur\">Minotaur</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Scrawny_Bugbear\" title=\"Scrawny Bugbear\">Scrawny Bugbear</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Severn\" title=\"Severn\">Severn</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Stimk\" title=\"Stimk\">Stimk</a>,  <a href=\"/wiki/Teghun\" title=\"Teghun\">Teghun</a></li></ul>\n</div> <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\"> Notes </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box bg3wiki-tooltip\">\n<ul><li>When used in combination with <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Great_Weapon_Fighting\" title=\"Great Weapon Fighting\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1f/Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp/25px-Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/1f/Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp/38px-Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/1f/Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp/50px-Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Great Weapon Fighting\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1f/Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp/25px-Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/1f/Great_Weapon_Fighting_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Great_Weapon_Fighting\" title=\"Great Weapon Fighting\">Great Weapon Fighting</a>, Great Weapon Fighting is applied before selecting the highest damage roll with this feat: Great Weapon Fighting will do a first roll and reroll if it is a 1 or 2, while Savage Attacker will then roll one more time for each roll and use the highest result.</li>\n<li>When making a melee <a href=\"/wiki/Attack_roll\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Attack roll\">attack roll</a>, this Passive Feature is known to affect damage riders (see <a href=\"/wiki/Damage_Mechanics\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Damage Mechanics\">Damage Mechanics</a>) such as <a href=\"/wiki/Divine_Smite\" title=\"Divine Smite\">Divine Smite</a>. Specifically, damage rolls for these damage riders are rolled twice for the higher result. Unknown if this mechanic interaction is bugged or intended.</li>\n<li>As of patch 7 this feat does now apply to <a href=\"/wiki/Sneak_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sneak Attack\">Sneak Attacks</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Blade_Flourish\" title=\"Blade Flourish\">Blade Flourishes</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Manoeuvres\" title=\"Manoeuvres\">Manoeuvres</a>.</li>\n<li>Each damage die is rolled twice independently, even for weapons that deal 2d6 damage.\n<ul><li>For example if a 2d6 weapon rolls 1 and 5 rerolled respectively into 3 and 4, the total damage would be 3 + 5 = 8 and not 7.</li></ul></li>\n<li>This feat essentially means you have <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Advantage\" title=\"Advantage\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fc/Advantage_Icon.png/28px-Advantage_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/fc/Advantage_Icon.png/42px-Advantage_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/fc/Advantage_Icon.png/55px-Advantage_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Advantage\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fc/Advantage_Icon.png/28px-Advantage_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/fc/Advantage_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Advantage\" title=\"Advantage\">Advantage</a> on your damage rolls. The average bonus to your damage becomes, depending on what dice the weapon uses (for the math, see <a href=\"/wiki/Advantage#Application:_Savage_Attacker\" title=\"Advantage\">the math section on the advantage page</a>):\n<ul><li>Weapon deals 1d4 damage: average bonus damage is 0.625 (+25.0%)</li>\n<li>Weapon deals 1d6 damage: average bonus damage is 0.972 (+27.8%)</li>\n<li>Weapon deals 1d8 damage: average bonus damage is 1.313 (+29.2%)</li>\n<li>Weapon deals 1d10 damage: average bonus damage is 1.650 (+30.0%)</li>\n<li>Weapon deals 1d12 damage: average bonus damage is 1.986 (+30.6%)</li>\n<li>Weapon deals 2d6 damage: average bonus damage is 1.944 (+27.8%)</li>\n<li>For example, the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-very-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Halberd_of_Vigilance\" title=\"Halberd of Vigilance\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/a/af/Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/a/af/Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/a/af/Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/a/af/Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/a/af/Halberd_PlusTwo_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Halberd_of_Vigilance\" title=\"Halberd of Vigilance\">Halberd of Vigilance</a> (1d10 slashing damage and 1d4 force damage) which was <a href=\"/wiki/Dip#Condition:_Dipped_in_Fire\" title=\"Dip\">dipped in fire</a> (1d4 fire damage) will, on average, do 1.65 + 0.625 + 0.625 = 2.9 (+27.6%) more damage with Savage Attacker.</li></ul></li>\n<li>When throwing weapons with the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Thrown\" title=\"Thrown\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/21/Thrown_Icon.png/25px-Thrown_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/21/Thrown_Icon.png/38px-Thrown_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/21/Thrown_Icon.png/50px-Thrown_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Thrown\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/21/Thrown_Icon.png/25px-Thrown_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/21/Thrown_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Thrown\" title=\"Thrown\">Thrown</a> property, Savage Attacker will apply to the roll for the base weapon damage, but not any additional damage riders such as <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-uncommon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ring_of_Flinging\" title=\"Ring of Flinging\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5a/Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/25px-Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/5a/Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/38px-Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/5a/Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/50px-Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5a/Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/25px-Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/5a/Ring_C_Silver_A_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Ring_of_Flinging\" title=\"Ring of Flinging\">Ring of Flinging</a>.</li></ul>\n</div>   \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714202016\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1762/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 16693/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 12065/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 22/200\nExpensive parser function count: 0/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1000/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 40/1000\nLua time usage: 0.011/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1031360/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   49.236      1 -total\n 98.30%   48.397      1 Template:Passive_feature_page\n 21.38%   10.529      2 Template:Item_icon\n 16.02%    7.888      3 Template:Icon_link\n 15.15%    7.457      1 Template:SmRarityItem\n 14.83%    7.304      3 Template:Icon_text\n 14.02%    6.904     18 Template:Trim\n 11.53%    5.678      1 Template:SAI\n 10.67%    5.254      1 Template:RarityItem\n  8.73%    4.297      7 Template:Ifempty\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:8373-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714202016 and revision id 285718. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}